        "start_xml_ordinal": 15868,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 613,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 271,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "In order to construct a boundary that can both generate waves and is weakly reflective a few simplifications are made. The boundary is considered to be a straight line. The local coordinate system is such that the x-axis is perpendicular to the boundary and directed positive inwards and the y-axis is parallel to the boundary. Locally, the bottom is approximated as flat and the wave motion is assumed to be linear."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 15881,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 615,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 273,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "At the boundary the free surface elevation and depth averaged velocity are the summation of the incoming and reflected signal"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 15928,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 617,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 275,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "Where both  and  are the mean free surface location and velocity which may vary on timescales that are much longer than the typical timescales of the incident and reflective signals."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "_staging/total-read/model-audit/XBeach/connectivity/nonhydro-read/body-field-recovery/body-cached.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 15993,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 619,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 277,
        "paragraph_id": null,
        "text": "The incident wave signal at the boundary is composed of N incoming long crested harmonic free linear waves. Each wave travels with its own celerity  along a straight ray in the direction. Along each wave ray a local coordinate system s,t  is prescribed with s parallel to the wave ray and t  perpendicular to the ray. The time varying depth averaged velocity due to harmonic k in the direction of s is denoted by. At a certain point on the boundary the total depth averaged velocity and surface elevation due to the incident waves is given by"
      }
    ],
    "table_cell": null,
    "text_method": "Saved display-field substitution plus w:t; equation objects are not transcribed."
  },
